-- title:
--   Unramified off the closed fibre persists under local base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $R'$ and $S$ be commutative rings, with $R$ and $R'$ local, let $R'$ be an $R$-algebra such that the ideal of $R'$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $R$ under the structure map is exactly the maximal ideal of $R'$, and let $S$ be an $R$-algebra which is finite as an $R$-module. Assume that for every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $S$ which is not maximal, the algebra $S$ over $R$ is unramified at $\mathfrak q$, i.e. the point $\mathfrak q$ of $\operatorname{Spec} S$ lies in `Algebra.unramifiedLocus R S`. The conclusion is that the same holds after base change to $R'$: for every prime ideal $\mathfrak Q$ of $R' \otimes_R S$ which is not maximal, the algebra $R' \otimes_R S$ over $R'$ is unramified at $\mathfrak Q$. No flatness, separability or Noetherian hypothesis is imposed, and nothing is asserted about the maximal primes on either side.
--
--   This is the local base-change stability of the property 'unramified away from the closed fibre' for a module-finite algebra over a local ring, the base change being required to carry the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal. It is used in the analysis of the completed local rings of the crossing model, via [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_moduleFinite_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_isGalois`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_moduleFinite_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_isGalois).
